THOUGHT: The error is that the copy constructor doesn’t guarantee initialization of the @NonNull field `elements` on all paths. `cloneState` can throw if `S` is null, and `elements` is not set before that. A simple fix is to validate `S` (throwing before any field access) and initialize `elements` to a non-null default (e.g., empty array) before calling `cloneState`. I’ll edit the file accordingly and then run the build to confirm that the specific NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/wala-util && sed -i '66,68c\  protected SparseIntSet(SparseIntSet S) {
    if (S == null) {
      throw new IllegalArgumentException("S == null");
    }
    // ensure elements is non-null before delegating to cloneState
    this.elements = new int[0];
    cloneState(S);
  }' src/main/java/com/ibm/wala/util/intset/SparseIntSet.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "SparseIntSet.java:66" new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

